# Shalean Engineering Standard

Read and follow `docs/engineering/SHALEAN_ENGINEERING_STANDARD.md` and the repository `AGENTS.md` before changing code.

## Mandatory workflow

- Work only on the current approved feature, fix, chore, docs or audit branch.
- Do not create another branch unless necessary; explain why first.
- Never develop directly on `main` or `staging`.
- Keep related changes together. Do not add unrelated refactors.
- Run local and relevant repository tests before pushing.
- Do not push or merge to `staging` after every commit.
- Do not merge to `main` unless the user explicitly authorizes it after required checks and staging verification.
- Create or update one final PR only when the task is materially complete.
- Minimize Vercel builds. Feature branches are intentionally ignored; use `staging` for completed acceptance testing and `main` for approved production releases.

## Safety

- Server-side authorization is the source of truth.
- Preserve least privilege and fail closed for unknown roles, permissions and scopes.
- Never expose secrets, service-role keys, payment credentials, customer data, cleaner identity documents or bank details.
- Do not weaken maker-checker, audit, payout, earnings, payment or booking-integrity controls.
- Never edit an applied production migration; create a forward migration.
- Prefer idempotent handling for payments, invoices, recurring bookings, notifications and payouts.
- Use integer cents for money calculations unless the approved domain model requires otherwise.
- Treat `Africa/Johannesburg` as the operational timezone unless an integration explicitly requires UTC.

## Before review

Report:

- Branch used
- Files changed
- Behaviour implemented
- Tests run and results
- Security, financial and database impact
- Environment changes
- Staging verification required or completed
- Risks and remaining work
